%% title: Exam papers: what each one needs first
%% desc: Exam papers come in three parts. Before the exam: the admit card needs a published seat plan and the routine notice needs a schedule. In the exam hall: the seat list, invigilator sheet and seat stickers need a published seat plan; the blank marks sheet needs the marks parts set up. After results: the tabulation needs results processed; the mark sheets, result certificate and merit certificate need results published.
flowchart LR
  subgraph B["Before the exam"]
    direction TB
    B1["Admit card<br/>published seat plan"]:::admin
    B2["Routine notice<br/>schedule"]:::admin
    B1 ~~~ B2
  end
  subgraph H["In the exam hall"]
    direction TB
    H1["Seat list<br/>published seat plan"]
    H2["Invigilator sheet<br/>published seat plan"]
    H3["Seat stickers<br/>published seat plan"]
    H4["Marks sheet<br/>marks parts set up"]
    H1 ~~~ H2
    H2 ~~~ H3
    H3 ~~~ H4
  end
  subgraph A["After results"]
    direction TB
    A1["Tabulation<br/>results processed"]:::done
    A2["Mark sheets<br/>results published"]:::done
    A3["Result certificate<br/>results published"]:::done
    A4["Merit certificate<br/>results published"]:::done
    A1 ~~~ A2
    A2 ~~~ A3
    A3 ~~~ A4
  end
  B ~~~ H
  H ~~~ A
  classDef admin fill:#fff4e6,stroke:#e8590c,color:#7a2e05
  classDef done fill:#ebfbee,stroke:#2b8a3e,color:#14411d
